-- 4. m41 a11_metric_power: M25's ISO-50 gain bug on real planes
   G = 0.11446886 is ISO/436.8; the corrected model is
   max(ISO,100)/436.8 = 0.22894 because Sony ISO 50 is an extended
   pull reading out at base-ISO gain (AGENTS M25 row, fixed 2a4f5c5).

  m41 a11 sigma_map on 119MSDCF @ 250 DN
      level   250.00 DN   g/rn used (0.11447, 4.2)  correct (0.22894, 4.2)
      modelled sd   3.7979 vs   5.3925 DN   ratio 0.7043x  (-29.57%)
      injected noise is 1/ratio too SMALL -> every detection claim is anti-conservative, every failure-to-detect claim is conservative and survives

  m41 a11 sigma_map on 119MSDCF @ 1200 DN
      level  1200.00 DN   g/rn used (0.11447, 4.2)  correct (0.22894, 4.2)
      modelled sd   8.2944 vs  11.7399 DN   ratio 0.7065x  (-29.35%)
      injected noise is 1/ratio too SMALL -> every detection claim is anti-conservative, every failure-to-detect claim is conservative and survives

-- 5. SYNTHESIS fact 130's ISO-50 temporal-sigma cap
   Fact 130 rules fact 88's 43.2-53.1 DN impossible because the
   model caps temporal sigma at 22.9 DN. That 22.9 was computed
   with the superseded g = 0.1145.

      level 4585 DN (fact 130's stated ROI-mean ceiling)
      cap with superseded g = 0.11447 : 22.91 DN   (fact 130 says 22.9)
      cap with corrected  g = 0.22894 : 32.41 DN
      fact 88's range 43.2-53.1 DN is still ABOVE the corrected cap by 1.33x-1.64x
      -> the digits move 1.41x; the CONCLUSION survives. FOOTNOTE.

-- 6. Is m41's fact 478 (the (1-rho) law) exposed?
   DERIVED: a11 scales both the shared and the independent noise
   draw by the same sigma_map. A global amplitude scalar therefore
   multiplies numerator and denominator of the recovery ratio
   alike and cancels -- the same algebra as facts 617/708, where a
   linear post-filter scales C and U by |H|^2 and ring FRC cannot
   move. So the (1-rho) SCALING is invariant to the gain error.
   The absolute recovery ratios of fact 477 are NOT protected by
   that argument and were not re-measured here.

